          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Lorck\",\"addressee\":\"Constance\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\\nJeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression is a direct, emphatic avowal that Lorck presently loves Constance. The immediate insistence that it is serious reinforces its truth-presenting force, regardless of whether his conception of love is healthy or sincere.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig, Constance  det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The focal words themselves avow a state and do not specify an undertaking. Lorck's adjacent offer to give Constance himself, his life and his soul is a separate expression and its promissory or relational force must not be transferred to “Jeg elsker dig.”\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg giver dig mig selv, mit Liv, min Sjæl, -\\nvil du ikke ta imod det?\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"Although Lorck speaks under intense affect, the focal expression is a deliberate avowal accompanied by an assertion of seriousness, not a reflex-like discharge beyond assertion.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"det er Alvor,\\nganske anderledes end jeg selv endog vidste.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, the expression's core force is adequately represented as an avowal of love under T. Its contextual persuasive purpose does not constitute a distinct core mode inadequately captured by T/P/E.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Jeg elsker dig\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Lorck repeats and intensifies his avowal after Constance has resisted his advances and reacted fearfully. He addresses her directly, insists that his love is serious, and then makes a separate offer of himself, his life and his soul.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression itself contains no undertaking. In the immediately following, separate utterance, Lorck offers himself, his life and his soul to Constance and asks her to accept; she answers “Nej, uf nej” and withdraws, so that offer receives explicit negative uptake. The scene supports genuine intense passion in Lorck, though it does not establish that his possessive and threatening conduct amounts to benevolent love.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The characters and passage are recognisable as likely coming from Amalie Skram's novel “Constance Ring”; that recognition was not used to add omitted plot information.\",\"limitations\":\"The judgment is confined to the marked occurrence and supplied scene. The scene strongly represents intense affect, but it cannot conclusively settle Lorck's sincerity, the quality of his feeling, or any broader relationship history beyond what is quoted.\"}"
